title: Explaining Paradigm exposed what it gets wrong about itself; two fix PRs merged the same night
summary: 'Research for the public hero pages (an evidence dossier and a teaching audit) found that Paradigm''s docs and generated files said things the product does not do. Two PRs fixed the first batch and merged into the integration branch feat/gnomon-dimensions: #101 (product) and #100 (docs). Review of #101 also uncovered a Stop-hook bug and a record-overwrite bug.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#shift'
  - '#ide-adapters'
  - '#hooks'
  - '#unique-record'
  - '#site'
  - '#readme'
learnings:
  - Text that describes a mechanism must be derived from the mechanism and pinned to it by a test, or it drifts into a new kind of wrong
  - A test that fails once in a thousand runs can be a data-loss bug with a one-in-a-thousand rate; read the id scheme before calling it a flake
  - 'Writing honest public copy is an effective audit: every sentence needs a source, and the sentences without one are the product''s defects'
  - Reviewers without a shell still find real bugs by reading; the orchestrator re-runs their claims before acting
